Fix the old-style signal handler signatures to match what sigaction(2)/signal(2)
expect. Modern glibc declares __sighandler_t as void (*)(int); the empty
parameter lists produced void (*)(), rejected by modern GCC under
-Werror (-Werror=incompatible-pointer-types).

